WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.573
Easy Fables. Part 5.

00:00:02.573 --> 00:00:04.134
The Thirsty Pigeon.

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:06.415
A pigeon was very thirsty.

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:09.189
She had flown a long way on a hot day.

00:00:09.189 --> 00:00:13.400
Then she saw a glass of water on a sign outside a shop.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.163
It was only a picture, but she did not know that.

00:00:17.163 --> 00:00:19.933
She flew toward it as fast as she could.

00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:23.336
She hit the sign very hard and fell to the ground.

00:00:23.336 --> 00:00:27.194
Her wing was hurt, and a man picked her up easily.

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:31.201
Do not be in such a hurry that you forget to look carefully.

00:00:31.201 --> 00:00:32.971
The Wolf and the Dog.

00:00:32.971 --> 00:00:36.253
A thin, hungry wolf met a fat dog.

00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:39.063
"You look very well," said the wolf.

00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:41.324
"Where do you find so much food?"

00:00:41.324 --> 00:00:44.007
"My job is easy," said the dog.

00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:46.007
"I watch the house at night.

00:00:46.007 --> 00:00:51.101
For that, the family gives me meat every day and a warm place to sleep.

00:00:51.101 --> 00:00:52.191
Come with me.

00:00:52.191 --> 00:00:53.807
You can have the same."

00:00:53.807 --> 00:00:55.802
The wolf was happy to go.

00:00:55.802 --> 00:01:00.438
But as they walked, he saw that the hair on the dog's neck was thin.

00:01:00.438 --> 00:01:03.289
"What happened to your neck?" he asked.

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:06.278
"Oh, that is nothing," said the dog.

00:01:06.278 --> 00:01:08.493
"During the day they tie me up.

00:01:08.493 --> 00:01:10.217
But I do not mind."

00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:12.736
"Then goodbye," said the wolf.

00:01:12.736 --> 00:01:17.046
"I would like to be hungry and free more than fat and tied up."

00:01:17.046 --> 00:01:19.455
Nothing is worth more than being free.

00:01:19.455 --> 00:01:21.623
The Man and His Two Wives.

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:24.600
Long ago, a man had two wives.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.317
One wife was young and the other was old.

00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:29.969
The man's hair was starting to turn white.

00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:32.415
The young wife did not like this.

00:01:32.415 --> 00:01:35.098
She did not want a husband who looked old.

00:01:35.098 --> 00:01:38.357
So every night she pulled out some of his white hairs.

00:01:38.357 --> 00:01:41.653
The old wife was happy to see his hair turn white.

00:01:41.653 --> 00:01:44.467
She did not want to look older than her husband.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:47.890
So every morning she pulled out some of his black hairs.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.646
Soon the man had no hair left at all.

00:01:50.646 --> 00:01:55.366
If you try to please everyone, you will have nothing left for yourself.

00:01:55.366 --> 00:01:57.152
The Boy and the Nuts.

00:01:57.152 --> 00:02:00.534
A boy put his hand into a jar full of nuts.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:03.231
He took as many as his hand could hold.

00:02:03.231 --> 00:02:07.117
But when he tried to pull his hand out, he could not.

00:02:07.117 --> 00:02:11.002
The opening of the jar was too small for his full hand.

00:02:11.002 --> 00:02:16.063
He did not want to drop any of the nuts, and he could not get his hand out.

00:02:16.063 --> 00:02:17.515
He began to cry.

00:02:17.515 --> 00:02:18.994
His mother saw him.

00:02:18.994 --> 00:02:21.964
"Do not try to take so many," she said.

00:02:21.964 --> 00:02:25.541
"Take only half, and your hand will come out easily.

00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:27.711
You can come back for more later."

00:02:27.711 --> 00:02:30.201
Do not try to do too much at once.

00:02:30.201 --> 00:02:32.509
The Donkey in the Lion's Skin.

00:02:32.509 --> 00:02:35.072
A donkey found the skin of a lion.

00:02:35.072 --> 00:02:37.893
He put it on and walked through the forest.

00:02:37.893 --> 00:02:41.090
All the animals were afraid and ran away from him.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.124
The donkey felt very strong and important.

00:02:44.124 --> 00:02:49.198
He was so pleased with himself that he opened his mouth and gave a loud cry.

00:02:49.198 --> 00:02:51.592
But it was not the cry of a lion.

00:02:51.592 --> 00:02:53.681
It was the voice of a donkey.

00:02:53.681 --> 00:02:56.230
A fox heard him and stopped running.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.181
She came back and laughed.

00:02:58.181 --> 00:03:01.378
"You almost made me afraid too," she said.

00:03:01.378 --> 00:03:03.447
"But then you opened your mouth."

00:03:03.447 --> 00:03:08.249
Fine clothes may hide a fool, but his words will show who he is.
